WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.169 --> 00:00:03.370
Okay, so in this section for nodal point,

2
00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.849
we're going to talk about tracked object creation.

3
00:00:05.849 --> 00:00:07.570
Now, we are going to do this in the engine,

4
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.410
so we're actually going to build our tracked object.

5
00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:10.490
But before we do,

6
00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:12.050
we want to see what it is that we

7
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.769
actually need for our tracked object creation.

8
00:00:14.769 --> 00:00:16.929
Now, we have already provided you with

9
00:00:16.929 --> 00:00:19.850
a OptiPuck track FBX which is going to

10
00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:21.969
match any motive tracking puck

11
00:00:21.969 --> 00:00:24.109
that you have if you're using the motive system.

12
00:00:24.109 --> 00:00:25.329
If your system is different,

13
00:00:25.329 --> 00:00:26.789
you will need to model

14
00:00:26.789 --> 00:00:29.769
your FBX object that you're going to be used for tracking.

15
00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:30.969
You're also going to need to make sure that

16
00:00:30.969 --> 00:00:32.130
any tracking system that you

17
00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.270
have has that model that's available.

18
00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:36.170
These models don't exist in the engine,

19
00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:38.090
but we are providing them for you as we have

20
00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:40.990
modeled them to use in our own system here.

21
00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:43.170
Now, let's go ahead and jump back into

22
00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:46.469
the engine so that we can start importing our FBX.

23
00:00:46.469 --> 00:00:47.829
Now, if you see here,

24
00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:49.969
I am in my calibration folder and I need

25
00:00:49.969 --> 00:00:52.409
another folder to make my objects

26
00:00:52.409 --> 00:00:54.869
for nodal point having a place to live.

27
00:00:54.869 --> 00:00:57.210
So let's go ahead and right-click and create

28
00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:59.770
a new folder and we're going to call this one nodal point.

29
00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:01.609
As I mentioned, this is where

30
00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:03.210
my nodal point objects are going to live.

31
00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.590
So once that's created, go ahead and double-click this open.

32
00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:08.049
Now, let's right-click so we can import

33
00:01:08.049 --> 00:01:10.989
to the engine our calibration object.

34
00:01:10.989 --> 00:01:12.769
So once you hit the import object,

35
00:01:12.769 --> 00:01:15.290
you are going to look for our OptiPuck track FBX,

36
00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.810
and you're going to go ahead and hit open to import this.

37
00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:20.409
This will bring up our FBX import options,

38
00:01:20.409 --> 00:01:22.049
and there's not really much that you want to

39
00:01:22.049 --> 00:01:24.530
make changes to in this list except if you

40
00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:26.409
haven't already built it correctly in

41
00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:28.849
centimeters and facing the front x-axis,

42
00:01:28.849 --> 00:01:29.849
just check these on.

43
00:01:29.849 --> 00:01:31.969
They won't really do anything if they're built correctly,

44
00:01:31.969 --> 00:01:33.370
but you can check them on in order

45
00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:34.790
to make sure that this is active.

46
00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:37.530
Now, by default, your import texture should be checked on,

47
00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.010
but if it's not, make sure that's

48
00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.810
checked on so that the texture comes with it,

49
00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:42.209
because we want to be able to modify

50
00:01:42.209 --> 00:01:44.430
that texture in order to change the color

51
00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:45.609
and make sure that this stands out

52
00:01:45.609 --> 00:01:47.170
a little bit better in the world.

53
00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:49.129
So let's go ahead and hit import all,

54
00:01:49.129 --> 00:01:50.049
and you're going to get a little bit of

55
00:01:50.049 --> 00:01:51.530
an error that comes up in here,

56
00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:54.129
and we're going to go ahead and ignore that,

57
00:01:54.129 --> 00:01:57.049
and then we're going to look for our OptiPuck track static mesh,

58
00:01:57.049 --> 00:01:58.489
and we're going to open this up.

59
00:01:59.019 --> 00:02:01.859
Now, we didn't get our material to come in here,

60
00:02:01.859 --> 00:02:03.540
so I'm going to type in a Lambert

61
00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:04.840
and see what we've got in here.

62
00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:06.219
I've got my wall Lambert,

63
00:02:06.219 --> 00:02:07.840
and I've got another one in here.

64
00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:08.939
Right now, I've assigned it,

65
00:02:08.939 --> 00:02:10.280
but I'm just going to locate this,

66
00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:13.300
which is going to be located in our NDC,

67
00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.819
under our NDC materials,

68
00:02:14.819 --> 00:02:16.419
and I'm going to do this in order to

69
00:02:16.419 --> 00:02:19.099
use an existing material that is already in here.

70
00:02:19.099 --> 00:02:20.180
Now, this material,

71
00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:21.840
I'm just going to change the name of this.

72
00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.939
So we're going to call this OptiPuck track,

73
00:02:23.939 --> 00:02:25.659
and we also want to move this

74
00:02:25.659 --> 00:02:27.939
into our Nodal Point folder,

75
00:02:27.939 --> 00:02:31.039
because we want to make sure that these are all kept together.

76
00:02:31.039 --> 00:02:33.439
So, since we're adding these two pieces in here,

77
00:02:33.439 --> 00:02:36.240
let's go ahead and make an alteration to my parameters.

78
00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.759
I want to choose a nice default color value in here.

79
00:02:38.759 --> 00:02:40.879
Let's go ahead and select the color value

80
00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:44.000
inside the material for our OptiPuck track,

81
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.840
and I'm going to choose a really bright green here.

82
00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.080
I'm going to really crank this up

83
00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.800
so it's really easy to see.

84
00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:51.740
So once that's done, I'm going to go ahead and hit OK,

85
00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:54.870
and then I'm going to apply and save.

86
00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:58.270
Now, if I come back over to my OptiPuck track mesh,

87
00:02:58.270 --> 00:02:59.789
and you'll see that my puck itself

88
00:02:59.789 --> 00:03:01.789
is actually going to be green as well,

89
00:03:01.789 --> 00:03:04.509
once I change the Lambert to match.

90
00:03:04.509 --> 00:03:07.509
And since we called this as M underscore Opti,

91
00:03:07.509 --> 00:03:10.009
that's going to bring this up, and let's connect that.

92
00:03:10.009 --> 00:03:11.270
Now, the reason that I wanted to make sure

93
00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:12.550
that this is that color

94
00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:14.150
is so that it stands a little bit easier.

95
00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:15.509
And if I look at this mesh, again,

96
00:03:15.509 --> 00:03:17.710
I want to point out that there is a bump on the front

97
00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:18.689
and not on the back

98
00:03:18.689 --> 00:03:21.110
so that you can see which direction is forward.

99
00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:23.990
Otherwise, all four corners here have to match.

100
00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:25.110
It's also going to allow you to see

101
00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:28.210
where we're going to be putting our center control.

102
00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:30.210
Now, once that's done, I'm going to go ahead and hit save,

103
00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.370
and I can close this window

104
00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:33.870
because I'm pretty much done in here.

105
00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:35.830
Now, again, I want to make sure that these get added

106
00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:37.289
because I'm using source control.

107
00:03:37.289 --> 00:03:38.930
So I'm going to go ahead and hit source control,

108
00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:39.770
mark for add.

109
00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.110
I want to make sure that this gets changed to a plus.

110
00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:43.530
Now, if it doesn't change to a plus

111
00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:44.889
because I'm in an active session,

112
00:03:44.889 --> 00:03:46.770
all I need to do to make sure that that happens

113
00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:50.409
is go in here and persist my session changes.

114
00:03:50.409 --> 00:03:52.289
Now, you can see all these changes that are in here.

115
00:03:52.289 --> 00:03:53.689
I'm going to go ahead and hit persist,

116
00:03:53.689 --> 00:03:55.250
and hopefully this goes through

117
00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.169
and makes those changes happen.

118
00:03:57.169 --> 00:03:59.330
Now, it did fail to persist with one error.

119
00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:00.930
I'm not going to worry about that error just now

120
00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:03.849
because I still got the add for the two components

121
00:04:03.849 --> 00:04:05.469
that I wanted to work with.

122
00:04:05.469 --> 00:04:07.430
Now, if I jump and take a look at my slides here,

123
00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:09.669
there is a next step in our tracked object creation.

124
00:04:09.669 --> 00:04:10.509
So as I mentioned,

125
00:04:10.509 --> 00:04:12.490
we are using that bright green that's in here,

126
00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:13.849
and I've got my tracked object.

127
00:04:13.849 --> 00:04:15.789
I do want to make sure that we are working through here.

128
00:04:15.789 --> 00:04:17.649
So things that we need to add to this

129
00:04:17.649 --> 00:04:19.730
is we need to add a component controller

130
00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:20.810
for the OptiPuck track

131
00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:22.649
that is assigning this to our component.

132
00:04:22.649 --> 00:04:24.730
And then I also need to add in

133
00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:28.850
some static mesh components for some calibration points.

134
00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:31.250
Now, let's go through and start by adding in

135
00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:34.089
our calibration points rather than our track section.

136
00:04:34.089 --> 00:04:35.970
So let's jump back to the engine.

137
00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:37.649
Okay, looking at our object,

138
00:04:37.649 --> 00:04:40.029
we need to make sure that this is already in the engine.

139
00:04:40.029 --> 00:04:41.730
So I'm going to take my tracked object.

140
00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:44.529
I'm going to make sure that I'm in the NDC level.

141
00:04:44.529 --> 00:04:45.970
Right now I'm in my persistent level.

142
00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:47.829
I need to make sure that I'm in my NDC level

143
00:04:47.829 --> 00:04:51.139
because this is going to be part of my NDC.

144
00:04:51.139 --> 00:04:52.240
So as I move in here,

145
00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:53.759
let's go ahead and move this into place,

146
00:04:53.759 --> 00:04:56.600
and then let's press F to focus in on it.

147
00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.959
Now, as I move this in place,

148
00:04:57.959 --> 00:05:00.500
I am going to want to be able to see what's happening

149
00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.199
right in the middle of my screen.

150
00:05:02.199 --> 00:05:03.480
I've got my front facing me,

151
00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:05.000
so I am looking in the front here,

152
00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.079
and this is exactly what I need.

153
00:05:07.079 --> 00:05:08.819
Now let's start by adding in components.

154
00:05:08.819 --> 00:05:10.220
I'm going to move over to my details panel

155
00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:11.519
while my object is selected.

156
00:05:11.519 --> 00:05:13.500
So I'm making sure that this is selected in my outliner.

157
00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.040
I'm going to go ahead and move my OptiPuck track

158
00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:18.170
to my offset actor.

159
00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:20.350
And one thing I need to do before that

160
00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:23.189
is I noticed that my mesh is set to static.

161
00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:25.509
I need to adjust that to movable.

162
00:05:25.509 --> 00:05:27.670
So I move over into my details panel,

163
00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:29.269
change that from static to movable,

164
00:05:29.269 --> 00:05:33.230
and now I can add this to my track offset actor.

165
00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:34.910
Now I need to add components.

166
00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:35.750
So as I mentioned here,

167
00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:38.089
I've got my OptiPuck track selected.

168
00:05:38.089 --> 00:05:39.709
I'm going to go ahead and hit add,

169
00:05:39.709 --> 00:05:42.870
and that's going to add a calibration point.

170
00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.310
So I've typed in calibration point,

171
00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.750
and I'm going to rename this CP underscore,

172
00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.629
BTM for bottom, and left.

173
00:05:48.629 --> 00:05:50.910
So my first one here is the bottom left.

174
00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:52.790
Now I'm going to need a couple more of these,

175
00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:55.629
so let's go ahead and just duplicate that.

176
00:05:55.629 --> 00:05:58.110
This one, I'm going to change the name to bottom right.

177
00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:01.149
So instead of L for left, I'm going to use R for right.

178
00:06:01.149 --> 00:06:04.360
I'm going to go ahead and duplicate that again.

179
00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:07.079
And this one, I'm going to rename center,

180
00:06:07.079 --> 00:06:08.959
and I'm going to just type out center.

181
00:06:08.959 --> 00:06:10.040
Now I'm going to go ahead

182
00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:12.579
and duplicate my bottom left again,

183
00:06:12.579 --> 00:06:15.839
and I'm going to change this from L1 to top left,

184
00:06:15.839 --> 00:06:18.480
and we're going to duplicate this just one more time.

185
00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.839
I'm going to call this one top right.

186
00:06:20.839 --> 00:06:22.319
So now I have each of these points here,

187
00:06:22.319 --> 00:06:25.399
but they are all located in the same position.

188
00:06:25.399 --> 00:06:26.680
Now they're going to need to be put

189
00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:28.579
into a specific location,

190
00:06:28.579 --> 00:06:32.279
and that offset position is going to need to align them

191
00:06:32.279 --> 00:06:35.279
with my actual OptiTrack point.

192
00:06:35.279 --> 00:06:38.480
So that alignment here is going to need to be adjusted

193
00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:40.079
in centimeters to this position.

194
00:06:40.079 --> 00:06:42.120
So let's start with all of them right now,

195
00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:43.879
although we can deselect our center,

196
00:06:43.879 --> 00:06:46.199
because our center is already in the center.

197
00:06:46.199 --> 00:06:48.319
So let's go with our bottom left.

198
00:06:48.319 --> 00:06:49.319
Now our location here,

199
00:06:49.319 --> 00:06:51.699
if I just go ahead and go 4.5 centimeters,

200
00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:53.860
and go this one 4.5 as well,

201
00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:57.079
and now you'll see that my point is pretty much lined up

202
00:06:57.079 --> 00:06:58.019
in that corner.

203
00:06:58.019 --> 00:07:00.540
Now it's not quite where I want it,

204
00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.300
so let's make another adjustment here

205
00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:05.740
and change that from 4.5 to 4.75,

206
00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:07.620
and do the same on this side here as well.

207
00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:09.860
So now they're both in this location.

208
00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:12.100
Now this is actually my top right,

209
00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:14.060
so let's go ahead and move this over

210
00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:17.699
by removing my top right and my bottom right from my set

211
00:07:17.699 --> 00:07:21.259
and on my Y-axis make these negative 4.75.

212
00:07:21.259 --> 00:07:23.100
So that's going to align these in the middle here

213
00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.339
a little bit better.

214
00:07:24.339 --> 00:07:26.899
Now your position may be a little bit different than mine

215
00:07:26.899 --> 00:07:28.420
just because it's facing this

216
00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.939
and I'm expecting a different change.

217
00:07:29.939 --> 00:07:31.300
But now that I've got these set up,

218
00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.180
I'm going to switch over to my bottom numbers

219
00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.699
that are in here, I've got them selected.

220
00:07:34.699 --> 00:07:36.379
They have multiple values in here,

221
00:07:36.379 --> 00:07:38.300
but this one I'm just going to go ahead and hit a negative

222
00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:40.339
and now they'll move to the bottom in here.

223
00:07:40.339 --> 00:07:42.079
So now if I cycle through each one of these,

224
00:07:42.079 --> 00:07:44.339
you can see them move in each of the corners

225
00:07:44.339 --> 00:07:46.819
and into the middle so that they're aligned correctly.

226
00:07:46.819 --> 00:07:49.660
And if I scroll around here and tumble around my model,

227
00:07:49.699 --> 00:07:52.339
you can see each one is lined pretty close to the center

228
00:07:52.339 --> 00:07:54.579
of each of these calibration points.

229
00:07:54.579 --> 00:07:56.899
Now, once that's done, I do need this object

230
00:07:56.899 --> 00:07:58.500
to actually be tracked to something.

231
00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:01.959
So with this selected, I do need to add in a new component.

232
00:08:01.959 --> 00:08:05.550
So that component is going to be my tracked object point.

233
00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:09.029
So for that, if we jump back to our slides briefly,

234
00:08:09.029 --> 00:08:11.430
right here is my tracked object creation

235
00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:12.910
for my Live Lake tracking.

236
00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:15.870
So for this, I go ahead and add in another component.

237
00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:18.490
So let's jump back to the engine here

238
00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:21.829
and I go in to make sure my OptiPuck track is selected

239
00:08:21.829 --> 00:08:24.170
and I hit add and I go Live Link

240
00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:26.730
and I'm going to go with another Live Link controller.

241
00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.310
So this Live Link component controller

242
00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:31.089
is going to be called Live Link LL underscore CC

243
00:08:31.089 --> 00:08:32.649
for Live Link component controller,

244
00:08:32.649 --> 00:08:36.409
OptiPuck and underscore TRK for track.

245
00:08:36.409 --> 00:08:39.570
Not quite so many Rs, we're not a tiger or a pirate,

246
00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:41.190
we're just going to keep that one track.

247
00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:43.889
Now with that selected, I am going to make sure

248
00:08:43.889 --> 00:08:46.490
that my subject representation gets changed here as well.

249
00:08:46.529 --> 00:08:48.149
So I'm just going to move right down here

250
00:08:48.149 --> 00:08:50.250
to my Live Link subject representation

251
00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:51.090
and if I go in here,

252
00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:53.049
you can already see that with my Live Link,

253
00:08:53.049 --> 00:08:54.850
I have several active objects

254
00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:57.970
because I've already created my Nodal Puck for tracking.

255
00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.029
So again, back in my details panel,

256
00:09:00.029 --> 00:09:01.429
